1
00:00:06,720 --> 00:00:09,580
Good morning, rise and shine, everyone!

2
00:00:09,980 --> 00:00:12,040
You're listening to Mariah Radio.

3
00:00:12,520 --> 00:00:16,197
Kai Harada here, keeping you
company on this beautiful morning.

4
00:00:16,280 --> 00:00:20,517
The day is shaping up to be a great one,
and I have just what the doctor ordered.

5
00:00:20,600 --> 00:00:22,640
So sit back, relax, and enjoy.

6
00:00:38,220 --> 00:00:41,677
As you know, I'm a man of loose!

7
00:00:41,760 --> 00:00:44,480
And I never believe in love?

8
00:01:08,420 --> 00:01:10,126
Well, we're back in business.

9
00:01:10,480 --> 00:01:13,717
The reception usually clears
up once you're past the tower.

10
00:01:13,800 --> 00:01:16,620
Anyway, is this your
first time visiting Mario?

11
00:01:17,100 --> 00:01:17,980
Sure is.

12
00:01:18,320 --> 00:01:19,614
Got anything to share?

13
00:01:19,700 --> 00:01:21,347
In terms of recommendations?

14
00:01:22,760 --> 00:01:26,180
Oh, the miso-marinated
beef tongue is real good.

15
00:01:27,080 --> 00:01:27,977
Anything suspicious?

16
00:01:28,060 --> 00:01:29,119
Strange incidents?

17
00:01:29,460 --> 00:01:30,400
Sorry, sir.

18
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:34,637
But I'm afraid I don't know much when
it comes to oddball stuff like that.

19
00:01:34,720 --> 00:01:37,720
Um, would you kindly remind
me of your destination?

20
00:01:38,520 --> 00:01:40,857
We're going to the front of the station.

21
00:01:40,940 --> 00:01:42,140
Right, almost there.

22
00:01:46,020 --> 00:01:47,280
Good freaking grief.

23
00:01:47,820 --> 00:01:50,540
I swear this better not
be what I think it is.

24
00:01:59,800 --> 00:02:01,957
It happened in April 1999.

25
00:02:02,040 --> 00:02:06,937
It was my first day of high school and I
was about to make two very bizarre friends.

26
00:02:07,020 --> 00:02:12,137
I was about to become a high School and
wondered what the others would be like.

27
00:02:12,220 --> 00:02:15,777
In case you were wondering,
my name's Koichi Hirosei.

28
00:02:15,860 --> 00:02:18,137
Though I guess it's not that important.

29
00:02:18,220 --> 00:02:21,580
Anyway, I was nervously
walking myself to class when...

30
00:02:29,180 --> 00:02:30,010
What?

31
00:02:30,093 --> 00:02:31,137
But didn't I just...

32
00:02:31,220 --> 00:02:33,617
And I thought all my stuff
went flying everywhere.

33
00:02:33,700 --> 00:02:35,171
What the heck's going on?

34
00:02:35,440 --> 00:02:38,360
Sorry, I wasn't paying attention. A giant!

35
00:02:38,620 --> 00:02:41,240
He's got to be over 190 centimeters tall!

36
00:02:41,600 --> 00:02:43,417
Hey, maybe you can help me out.

37
00:02:43,500 --> 00:02:47,206
Here's the thing, I've come here
to find the Higashkata family.

38
00:02:47,940 --> 00:02:48,770
Higashikata?

39
00:02:48,853 --> 00:02:49,683
Let's see.

40
00:02:49,766 --> 00:02:51,237
Maybe an address will jog your memory.

41
00:02:51,320 --> 00:02:53,460
Does Joseonji-16 ring a bell?

42
00:02:53,860 --> 00:02:55,080
Jotaro Kujo.

43
00:02:55,620 --> 00:02:59,357
You can get to Joseonji pretty easily
by taking the number three bus.

44
00:02:59,440 --> 00:03:01,717
It won't be long before
another one comes around.

45
00:03:01,800 --> 00:03:02,630
Thanks, kid.

46
00:03:04,260 --> 00:03:06,980
The first guy that I met was Jotaro Kujo.

47
00:03:07,460 --> 00:03:11,225
Later on, I found out he was 28
years old and a marine explorer.

48
00:03:11,660 --> 00:03:12,490
Apparently,

49
00:03:12,573 --> 00:03:16,669
academics knew him best for his outstanding
research in the field of ecology.

50
00:03:17,420 --> 00:03:20,697
There's this fierceness about him,
but he also seems really intellectual.

51
00:03:20,780 --> 00:03:21,610
Wow.

52
00:03:22,620 --> 00:03:24,777
Hey, you another freshman, little man?

53
00:03:24,860 --> 00:03:26,978
Aren't you gonna introduce yourself?

54
00:03:27,180 --> 00:03:28,121
Right, yes, sir.

55
00:03:28,360 --> 00:03:30,020
I'm Koichi Hirose. Freshman.

56
00:03:30,120 --> 00:03:30,950
Good morning, sir.

57
00:03:31,033 --> 00:03:32,020
Nice to meet you.

58
00:03:32,200 --> 00:03:34,300
Yeah, that's more like it, runt.

59
00:03:35,500 --> 00:03:37,460
Man, that was a close one.

60
00:03:37,840 --> 00:03:39,617
You don't have to worry about them.

61
00:03:39,700 --> 00:03:42,317
I'm sure they'll find a different
bus and go about their business.

62
00:03:42,400 --> 00:03:44,157
What do you think you're doing, dickface?

63
00:03:44,240 --> 00:03:45,711
Who do you think you are?

64
00:03:47,480 --> 00:03:48,917
Well, if you really must know,

65
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:52,577
it seems this little turtle I found
just woke up from hibernation.

66
00:03:52,660 --> 00:03:54,580
But turtles give me the willies.

67
00:03:54,740 --> 00:03:57,097
It takes all my courage to
even touch their shells.

68
00:03:57,180 --> 00:04:00,097
So I thought today would be a good
day to finally conquer my fears.

69
00:04:00,180 --> 00:04:01,677
Buddy, does it look like I give a shit?

70
00:04:01,760 --> 00:04:02,900
Get up, you weirdo.

71
00:04:13,340 --> 00:04:16,928
Well, now, you've got some hype
for such a pathetic freshman.

72
00:04:17,060 --> 00:04:18,236
But here's the deal.

73
00:04:18,340 --> 00:04:20,877
You can dress like a puppet
freak if you want to.

74
00:04:20,960 --> 00:04:23,697
But first you have to pay
your respects to us, got it?

75
00:04:23,780 --> 00:04:25,427
Can you not do that, please?

76
00:04:25,540 --> 00:04:27,037
Reptiles really freak me out.

77
00:04:27,120 --> 00:04:28,414
They're all so creepy.

78
00:04:28,860 --> 00:04:31,978
Just who do you think you're
smirking at, pretty boy?

79
00:04:34,840 --> 00:04:35,781
Forgive me, sir.

80
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:37,797
I didn't know how things were done.

81
00:04:37,880 --> 00:04:38,917
That's kind of funny,

82
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:40,897
because I've put a lot
of guys in the hospital

83
00:04:40,980 --> 00:04:43,337
whose last words were
the exact same as yours.

84
00:04:43,420 --> 00:04:45,577
You need to learn some respect, dumbass!

85
00:04:45,660 --> 00:04:48,601
Unless you want to end up
like this stupid turtle!

86
00:04:50,060 --> 00:04:51,880
Man, this guy is heartless.

87
00:04:52,020 --> 00:04:53,785
But hey, I'm feeling merciful.

88
00:04:54,140 --> 00:04:56,957
Leave your jacket and pants with
us, and you get to walk away.

89
00:04:57,040 --> 00:04:57,917
Your cash, too!

90
00:04:58,000 --> 00:04:58,830
Right.

91
00:04:58,913 --> 00:04:59,743
Sorry for the trouble.

92
00:04:59,826 --> 00:05:04,015
A shaman had to go down this way, but
what did he expect in that get-up?

93
00:05:04,400 --> 00:05:06,020
Though it pisses me off,

94
00:05:06,140 --> 00:05:08,777
is that he can just sit back and
watch them pulverize a turtle.

95
00:05:08,860 --> 00:05:10,160
I got an idea, pussy.

96
00:05:10,420 --> 00:05:12,302
Why don't you tell us your name?

97
00:05:12,820 --> 00:05:13,650
Right.

98
00:05:13,733 --> 00:05:14,563
Class 1B.

99
00:05:14,646 --> 00:05:16,660
I'm Josuke Higashikata.

100
00:05:19,560 --> 00:05:20,440
Say what?

101
00:05:20,620 --> 00:05:21,880
Josuke Higashikata?

102
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:24,720
It says Joe and Joe.

103
00:05:25,320 --> 00:05:26,150
Josuke, huh?

104
00:05:26,233 --> 00:05:29,137
Well, if you ask me, Jojo
has a much better ring to it.

105
00:05:29,220 --> 00:05:30,220
Oh, uh, thanks.

106
00:05:30,460 --> 00:05:32,284
That's very kind of you to say.

107
00:05:32,580 --> 00:05:34,777
Shut your trap and take
off the damn jacket!

108
00:05:34,860 --> 00:05:36,477
Or didn't you notice the bus is here?

109
00:05:36,560 --> 00:05:40,913
If you don't hurry it up, I swear to
God I'll chop off that fogly cowlick!

110
00:05:41,040 --> 00:05:42,177
Did you hear what I said?

111
00:05:42,260 --> 00:05:43,090
Hurry it up!

112
00:05:43,173 --> 00:05:45,540
Sure, but first...

113
00:05:46,260 --> 00:05:47,090
Question.

114
00:05:47,173 --> 00:05:50,355
Could you repeat what you
just said about my hair, sir?

115
00:05:54,940 --> 00:05:55,820
A stand?

116
00:06:01,020 --> 00:06:02,860
My nose! My teeth!

117
00:06:03,560 --> 00:06:06,617
Talk shit about my hair and
you'll see a different side of me.

118
00:06:06,700 --> 00:06:09,297
A side that'll make you
feel pain like never before.

119
00:06:09,380 --> 00:06:12,337
So what was that about my hair
looking like a motley toupee?

120
00:06:12,420 --> 00:06:13,250
Huh?

121
00:06:13,333 --> 00:06:14,163
What are you talking about?

122
00:06:14,246 --> 00:06:15,076
No one said!

123
00:06:15,159 --> 00:06:17,640
I know what I heard,
dammit! What happened?

124
00:06:17,860 --> 00:06:19,977
That pump went flying through the air!

125
00:06:20,060 --> 00:06:22,119
There's no denying what I just saw.

126
00:06:22,240 --> 00:06:23,560
That was a stand.

127
00:06:29,220 --> 00:06:30,050
What?

128
00:06:30,133 --> 00:06:32,147
It's like the turtle's
cuts were never there.

129
00:06:34,420 --> 00:06:35,920
What the hell's going on?

130
00:06:36,100 --> 00:06:38,377
Your nose and teeth
are healing themselves!

131
00:06:38,460 --> 00:06:40,140
Look at that! He's fixed!

132
00:06:40,240 --> 00:06:42,887
Yeah, I guess, but why
is his face all weird?

133
00:06:43,080 --> 00:06:44,960
It looks totally different now.

134
00:06:45,740 --> 00:06:46,570
What is it?

135
00:06:46,653 --> 00:06:47,717
What happened to my face?

136
00:06:47,800 --> 00:06:48,630
Well, what?

137
00:06:49,520 --> 00:06:51,049
You've really done it now.

138
00:06:51,260 --> 00:06:54,217
You made me touch something that
I didn't want to lay a finger on.

139
00:06:54,300 --> 00:06:57,700
So how exactly do you plan
on making it up to me, huh?

140
00:07:00,300 --> 00:07:01,535
Wait, come back here!

141
00:07:01,620 --> 00:07:02,457
You can't leave!

142
00:07:02,540 --> 00:07:04,720
What happened to my nose? Guys, wait!

143
00:07:05,200 --> 00:07:06,560
They were a hassle.

144
00:07:07,180 --> 00:07:08,580
And this guy...

145
00:07:18,560 --> 00:07:19,600
Holy shit!

146
00:07:20,700 --> 00:07:22,582
Oh, it's just that turtle again.

147
00:07:24,240 --> 00:07:25,400
So I was right.

148
00:07:25,760 --> 00:07:27,877
Somehow, the turtle's completely healed.

149
00:07:27,960 --> 00:07:29,860
Josuke Higashkata.

150
00:07:30,240 --> 00:07:32,300
You were born in the year 1983.

151
00:07:33,100 --> 00:07:34,540
Mother's name, Tomoko.

152
00:07:34,900 --> 00:07:37,700
She was 21, attending university in Tokyo.

153
00:07:38,540 --> 00:07:40,897
This town's the only
home you've ever known.

154
00:07:40,980 --> 00:07:46,080
But everything changed in 1987, when you
came down with a mysterious fever at age 4.

155
00:07:46,860 --> 00:07:50,180
For 50 days, you were a
knock away from death's door.

156
00:07:51,260 --> 00:07:52,960
Your father's name is...

157
00:07:53,480 --> 00:07:54,420
Good grief.

158
00:07:54,700 --> 00:07:56,037
How'd I get mixed up in this?

159
00:07:56,120 --> 00:07:59,640
The name of your father is Joseph Joestar.

160
00:08:01,720 --> 00:08:05,760
He's 78 now, and the
founder of Joestar Realty.

161
00:08:06,360 --> 00:08:07,740
The Joseph Joestar?

162
00:08:08,120 --> 00:08:10,296
He's that American real estate mogul.

163
00:08:10,520 --> 00:08:12,397
Don't worry, the old man's fine.

164
00:08:12,480 --> 00:08:15,477
But one day I was looking into
how to divide his properties.

165
00:08:15,560 --> 00:08:19,442
That's when I discovered you, his
son, living right here in Japan.

166
00:08:20,100 --> 00:08:22,180
Even the old man had no idea.

167
00:08:22,540 --> 00:08:24,040
Piece of shit that he is.

168
00:08:24,800 --> 00:08:27,757
The bastard always said his
wife was his one and only.

169
00:08:27,840 --> 00:08:31,320
Then I find out he had an affair
at the ripe old age of 62.

170
00:08:31,940 --> 00:08:33,800
And the product of it is you.

171
00:08:34,100 --> 00:08:36,453
Sorry, guess I shouldn't have said that.

172
00:08:36,560 --> 00:08:38,320
My name is Jotaro Kujo.

173
00:08:38,660 --> 00:08:44,040
Which means, since he's my grandfather,
I'm technically your nephew. Bizarre, huh?

174
00:08:44,580 --> 00:08:45,410
Nephew?

175
00:08:46,300 --> 00:08:47,340
Huh? Pleasure.

176
00:08:49,220 --> 00:08:50,920
We can talk on the way.

177
00:08:55,080 --> 00:08:57,337
So, there you have it. Eventually,

178
00:08:57,420 --> 00:09:01,217
you're going to find yourself in possession
of a third of the old man's inheritance.

179
00:09:01,300 --> 00:09:03,577
That's the message I
came here to tell you.

180
00:09:03,660 --> 00:09:04,837
I hate to lay this on you,

181
00:09:04,920 --> 00:09:07,677
but this affair has turned the
Joestar family upside down.

182
00:09:07,760 --> 00:09:11,960
Er, upside down? Are you
serious? I am. My grandma,

183
00:09:12,200 --> 00:09:14,977
Susie Q, is the angriest she's
ever been in their entire marriage,

184
00:09:15,060 --> 00:09:17,119
and they've been together 61 years.

185
00:09:17,580 --> 00:09:18,410
What?

186
00:09:18,493 --> 00:09:19,323
Please forgive me!

187
00:09:19,406 --> 00:09:20,236
This is all my fault!

188
00:09:20,620 --> 00:09:22,620
Hey, there's no need to freak out.

189
00:09:22,780 --> 00:09:25,309
Why are you apologizing
in the first place?

190
00:09:25,700 --> 00:09:26,530
Well, I...

191
00:09:26,900 --> 00:09:29,997
I'd hate to be the cause of
the family falling apart.

192
00:09:30,080 --> 00:09:33,797
Whenever the subject came up, Mom
told me she was deeply in love.

193
00:09:33,880 --> 00:09:36,409
Knowing that she had
that is enough for me.

194
00:09:36,500 --> 00:09:37,637
Could you tell my dad?

195
00:09:37,720 --> 00:09:39,420
I mean, Mr. Joestar.

196
00:09:39,820 --> 00:09:43,080
He doesn't need to concern
himself with us. Thank you.

197
00:09:43,480 --> 00:09:44,715
What's with this kid?

198
00:09:45,100 --> 00:09:48,394
I came here ready to be decked
on behalf of the old man.

199
00:09:48,520 --> 00:09:51,557
But instead of being angry,
he's the one apologizing to me.

200
00:09:51,640 --> 00:09:55,940
Look, it's Josuke! Yeah, it is!
Hey, Josuke! What a coincidence!

201
00:09:56,560 --> 00:09:57,977
Let's go to class together!

202
00:09:58,060 --> 00:09:59,857
Your hair is looking glorious as ever!

203
00:09:59,940 --> 00:10:00,770
It's so great!

204
00:10:00,920 --> 00:10:03,357
You're so different from
the other guys at school!

205
00:10:03,440 --> 00:10:07,097
That's great, but we're actually in
the middle of an important chat, so...

206
00:10:07,180 --> 00:10:08,010
Aw, come on!

207
00:10:08,093 --> 00:10:09,917
If you don't hurry, you're
gonna be late for school!

208
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:11,059
We can talk later!

209
00:10:11,260 --> 00:10:12,201
Earth to Josuke.

210
00:10:12,480 --> 00:10:14,457
We haven't finished our business yet.

211
00:10:14,540 --> 00:10:15,897
Get the groupies out of here.

212
00:10:15,980 --> 00:10:17,097
Who the hell's this guy?

213
00:10:17,180 --> 00:10:20,827
Hey, you can cackle like hens
about his hair on your own time.

214
00:10:22,100 --> 00:10:24,657
This guy has no idea the
beast he's just released.

215
00:10:24,740 --> 00:10:26,975
Why'd he talk about his hair that way?

216
00:10:28,060 --> 00:10:28,890
Bastard.

217
00:10:29,240 --> 00:10:32,317
Do you want to repeat what
you just said about my hair?

218
00:10:32,400 --> 00:10:33,677
Oh, this isn't good.

219
00:10:33,760 --> 00:10:34,757
You don't have to tell me.

220
00:10:34,840 --> 00:10:38,657
The one thing that sets Josuke off like
nothing else is someone insulting his hair.

221
00:10:38,740 --> 00:10:40,637
This is just what happened before.

222
00:10:40,720 --> 00:10:42,240
Hold on a minute, Josuke.

223
00:10:42,500 --> 00:10:45,088
I wasn't trying to take
a shot at your hair.

224
00:10:47,520 --> 00:10:49,160
Damn, here he comes!

225
00:10:53,720 --> 00:10:55,420
Josuke, no! He's bleeding!

226
00:10:55,920 --> 00:10:57,280
Do you see it, Josuke?

227
00:10:57,720 --> 00:10:59,120
This is called a stand.

228
00:10:59,600 --> 00:11:02,071
It's a physical manifestation of the soul.

229
00:11:02,520 --> 00:11:04,402
Joseph has one of these as well.

230
00:11:05,360 --> 00:11:08,000
Only a stand user can see another stand.

231
00:11:08,500 --> 00:11:12,677
You know, it pisses me off when someone
decides to badmouth my pride and joy.

232
00:11:12,760 --> 00:11:14,580
It really grinds my gears!

233
00:11:18,340 --> 00:11:20,520
So that's what his stand looks like.

234
00:11:24,960 --> 00:11:26,880
This kid's power is unreal.

235
00:11:27,320 --> 00:11:31,673
Don't know if you realize this, nephew,
but you left your chest wide open!

236
00:11:32,040 --> 00:11:32,870
Enough!

237
00:11:34,060 --> 00:11:35,180
Where did he...?

238
00:11:38,120 --> 00:11:39,200
How'd that happen?

239
00:11:39,420 --> 00:11:40,297
What the heck is going on?

240
00:11:40,380 --> 00:11:41,210
Why, Hugh?

241
00:11:41,320 --> 00:11:42,177
When did...?

242
00:11:42,260 --> 00:11:43,400
Josuke!

243
00:11:44,780 --> 00:11:45,610
Josuke!

244
00:11:46,020 --> 00:11:48,117
Shut your mouths and
get the hell out of here

245
00:11:48,200 --> 00:11:50,788
before your whiny
bitching makes me angrier.

246
00:11:52,500 --> 00:11:53,330
Okay.

247
00:11:54,100 --> 00:11:55,537
They must know each other.

248
00:11:55,620 --> 00:11:56,740
He's kind of scary.

249
00:11:57,260 --> 00:11:59,100
Yeah, but in a hot way.

250
00:12:00,400 --> 00:12:01,230
Unreal.

251
00:12:01,313 --> 00:12:02,440
I don't understand.

252
00:12:02,800 --> 00:12:03,918
What just happened?

253
00:12:04,480 --> 00:12:06,715
I can't wrap my head around any of it.

254
00:12:07,660 --> 00:12:08,800
It's been a while.

255
00:12:09,380 --> 00:12:10,760
Ten years to be exact.

256
00:12:12,020 --> 00:12:14,377
I only managed to stop
time for half a second.

257
00:12:14,460 --> 00:12:17,157
I doubt we would have killed
each other if I hadn't,

258
